1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,260
One more thing.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:05,700
Dash Forge has been published to mainnet.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,760
This is not a DCG product but Dash Forge

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,140
is now deployed.

5
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:13,580
You can go to forge.dashhq.org and

6
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:19,220
you can deploy and push your own repo

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,960
directly on Dash Platform or using

8
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:26,660
S3 buckets or IPFS if you don't want

9
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:29,370
to pay the storage on Dash Platform.

10
00:00:29,370 --> 00:00:31,410
The way that it works is you download

11
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:33,410
an extension to Git, you install that

12
00:00:33,410 --> 00:00:35,650
extension and then that allows you

13
00:00:35,650 --> 00:00:38,050
to clone and push these repos just

14
00:00:38,050 --> 00:00:39,710
like you would normally.

15
00:00:40,170 --> 00:00:42,150
You can move stuff over from GitHub,

16
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:46,010
you can import issues and PRs, et cetera, from GitHub.

17
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:47,430
The really cool thing about this is

18
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:49,720
there isn't anything that you have to trust.

19
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:51,320
If you use the extension, everything

20
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:54,420
pulls directly from Dash Platform and

21
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:57,250
then IPFS or S3 or however you configure it.

22
00:00:57,250 --> 00:01:01,630
So this is a Dash Forge and so far

23
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:04,350
there is one Git repo on there and

24
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:06,120
that is Dash Forge itself.

25
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:09,560
The code here is hosted on IPFS and

26
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,160
all of the metadata is of course stored

27
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,390
on Dash Platform.

28
00:01:13,390 --> 00:01:16,730
So this is a repo under a data contract

29
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:20,230
and you can see all of the information about it.

30
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:22,110
We can look into this contract and

31
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:25,270
you can see everything that has happened so far.

